      ":question/problem": "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0\\}.\n$$",
